{
  "version": "2026-08-16T10:00",
  "changelog": [
    {
      "version": "2026-08-16T10:00",
      "change": "Split counters into a classified and a published census; made baseFirstEzhuthu the second and final partition key and dropped length from the partition table; added partitionKeys and ezhuthuIndex; dropped the ezhuthu column from the row; renamed provenance rowsIn / factsOut to observations / facts.",
      "why": "Row 11, the first writer. The publish policy commits four servable classes of ten, so a single counter would have made the withheld classes unprovable - classified counts the whole population and published counts the files, and publication is all-or-nothing per class, so 'nothing was discarded' is a checkable statement rather than a claim. The measured layout is one file per (wordClass, base first ezhuthu) at 241 files and a 2.2 MiB largest file, so the length key it was authored with addresses nothing and a partition key that is sometimes absent is worse than one that is always there. ezhuthu goes for the reason freqRank went: it is segment(word), a pure function of a published column, and storing a derived value is a drift surface as well as 35.4 B a row. observations / facts are what the store can actually prove about a source; rowsIn read as raw rows and no stage keeps that."
    },
    {
      "version": "2026-08-16",
      "change": "Added notAWord to the WordClass vocabulary.",
      "why": "Row 9a - the classifier had no verdict for a surface that is not a word at all, so 641,819 scrape artifacts wore real classes: repeated aytham as loanword, leading-dot strings as inflected, a 1,212-ezhuthu paragraph as suspectedTypo. notAWord is a CONFIDENT NEGATIVE and is deliberately distinct from unclassified, which is an ABSENT verdict - collapsing them would destroy the only counters that say whether the classifier works. Additive: every existing row still validates, and selection stays an allow-list so nothing reaches a player by omission."
    },
    {
      "version": "2026-08-14",
      "change": "Initial lexicon contracts: the LexiconEntry row shape and the Lexicon meta document (provenance, per-class counters, partition table).",
      "why": "Row 3 - contracts before logic (Holy Law #3): the all-words artifact that replaces the corpus funnel gets its typed shape before any stage reads or writes it."
    }
  ],
